                        "glosses": [
                            "A type of fig, Ficus sycomorus, native to the Middle East; the sycamore tree of the Bible."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "663abc05-c63c-4afc-9599-bffce3d35f73",
                                "sense_id": "4b09ef57-b439-32c1-85b1-0b706086bd71",
                                "text": "The Sycomore was and is one of the common trees of Egypt, and its wood was employed for the manufacture of mummy cases, and for doors, boxes, and all articles of furniture. […] So valuable was this tree that David appointed a special overseer “over the olive trees and sycomore trees that were in the low plains” (1 Chron. xxvii. 28) […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ffaf5ad-818a-4b24-bf6d-e403532b5f07",
                                "sense_id": "4b09ef57-b439-32c1-85b1-0b706086bd71",
                                "text": "And the king made siluer to be in Ierusalem as stones, and Cedars made he to be as the Sycomore trees, that are in the vale for abundance."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
